# Build output IS committed. A git install used to compile `lib/` through a
# `prepare` script, but pnpm refuses a git dependency's lifecycle scripts until
# the installing user allowlists that exact URL and commit SHA, so every install
# stopped at an approval prompt and every new commit invalidated the approval.
# Committing `lib/` removes the script, and `npm test` fails when the artifacts
# drift from `src/`. Rebuild before committing a source change.

# Dependencies. `package-lock.json` is committed so an install resolves the
# exact graph this release was built and tested against; `npm ci` reproduces it.
node_modules/

# Packed tarballs from `npm pack`.
*.tgz

# Editor and OS residue.
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.tsbuildinfo
*.log

# Local DSH data directories a test run may create (`HOME`, `DSH_HOME`).
.dsh-home/
